  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="&quot;JIA KUI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jia Kui, born in 174 and died around 230, was a military general and official during the late Eastern Han dynasty and the Three Kingdoms period, serving under the state of Cao Wei. He was enfeoffed as a Secondary Marquis for his work in preparing his jurisdictions for battle and ensuring they were well-supplied."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XIANGLING COUNTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xiangling County, part of Hedong Commandery, is the birthplace of Jia Kui, located in present-day Xiangfen County, Shanxi."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAO WEI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cao Wei was a state during the Three Kingdoms period, under which Jia Kui served as a military general and official."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIFEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lifen is mentioned as the birthplace of Jia Kui in some documents, corresponding to present-day Xiangfen County, Shanxi."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WANG GUAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wang Guan, died in 260, was an official of the state of Cao Wei during the Three Kingdoms period, serving as a Writing Assistant and County Prefect."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUN QUAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sun Quan was a ruler of the state of Wu during the Three Kingdoms period, who honored Gu Yong with the posthumous title 'Marquis Su' after his death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sun Quan was the ruler of the state of Wu during the Three Kingdoms period, who honored Gu Yong with the posthumous title 'Marquis Su'."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GU YONG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gu Yong was a respected official during the Three Kingdoms period, known for his abstinence from alcohol and maintaining proper conduct."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JIA QU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jia Qu is the original name of Jia Kui, who later changed his name to Jia Kui. He was a military general and official during the late Eastern Han dynasty and the Three Kingdoms period."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liu is mentioned as the spouse of Jia Kui, though her full name is not provided."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GAOTANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gaotang is mentioned as one of the counties where Wang Guan served as the County Prefect."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YANGQUAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Yangquan is mentioned as one of the counties where Wang Guan served as the County Prefect."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zan is mentioned as one of the counties where Wang Guan served as the County Prefect."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ren is mentioned as one of the counties where Wang Guan served as the County Prefect."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAO CAO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cao Cao was a prominent figure during the late Eastern Han dynasty and the founder of the state of Cao Wei. He summoned Wang Guan to serve in his administration."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAO PI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cao Pi was the son of Cao Cao and later became the emperor of the state of Cao Wei, recalling Wang Guan to the capital."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NANDUN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LOCATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nandun is a location that was occupied by Wang Ji and later by Guanqiu Jian."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nandun is mentioned as a place where Wang Ji was sent to occupy, though the exact location is not specified."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;XU HUANG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xu Huang is a character who engages in a conversation with Guan Yu about the art of war."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xu Huang is mentioned in the context of a conversation with Guan Yu, though no specific details are provided about his role or background."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUAN YU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Guan Yu is a character who is advised to find his own inner strength and engage in battle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Guan Yu is mentioned in the context of a conversation with Xu Huang, though no specific details are provided about his role or background."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNASTY WARRIORS 8&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dynasty Warriors 8 is a video game series featuring characters like Guan Yu and Xu Huang."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dynasty Warriors 8 is referenced in the context of a conversation between Xu Huang and Guan Yu, though no specific details are provided about the game or the characters within it."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASTER GUAN YU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Master Guan Yu is a character who is advised to follow his own path in the art of war."</data>
      <data key="d2">ramdocs-0303-b6e99ec183fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WANG JI&quot;">
